\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9.3}{\ignorespaces Top panel: The choice of OFI lens power affects the combination of OMx1 and OMx2 power that is required for 100\% mode-matching. Bottom panel: The best choice of OFI lens corresponds to where the Gouy phase separation between the pair of OMx1 and OMx2 is closest to \ang {45}. The most Gouy phase separation between OMx1 and OMx2 achievable by this layout is \ang {43}.\relax }}{115}{figure.caption.148}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterlenschoice}{{9.3}{115}{Top panel: The choice of OFI lens power affects the combination of OMx1 and OMx2 power that is required for 100\% mode-matching. Bottom panel: The best choice of OFI lens corresponds to where the Gouy phase separation between the pair of OMx1 and OMx2 is closest to \ang {45}. The most Gouy phase separation between OMx1 and OMx2 achievable by this layout is \ang {43}.\relax }{figure.caption.148}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9.4}{\ignorespaces Astigmatism is a source of loss. When designing this layout, to explore how sensitive it was to astigmatism, the AOI for the curved mirrors was altered. Using equation (\ref  {eq:bhd_for_ligo_mm_loss}), the loss was computed. This effect is negligible up to 10\si {\degree } after which it starts to become significant compared to the losses summarised in Table \ref  {tab:HAM6_losses}.\relax }}{116}{figure.caption.149}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterastigmatism}{{9.4}{116}{Astigmatism is a source of loss. When designing this layout, to explore how sensitive it was to astigmatism, the AOI for the curved mirrors was altered. Using equation (\ref {eq:bhd_for_ligo_mm_loss}), the loss was computed. This effect is negligible up to 10\si {\degree } after which it starts to become significant compared to the losses summarised in Table \ref {tab:HAM6_losses}.\relax }{figure.caption.149}{}}
